00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:47.150
- I

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:52.170
took some training actually when
I worked at Health Net,

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:55.305
giving a presentation to our
execs. And what was helpful was

00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.195
really the power poses that they
had us do, which are so

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.480
weird when you start
doing them. Yeah,

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.460
mark something like
that, like the power

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:10.130
you get in your chair. You
get all, make your body big.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:13.020
There's different ones.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:16.470
I'm sure many of you have
heard of those and do them.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:18.180
But for me that helps a lot

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.490
to get rid of jitters
or something like--

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.950
it's almost like doing yoga
in a way because you're stretching

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:26.190
your body, you're breathing,
getting the blood flowing.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:30.435
But aside from that,
the other thing that

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:34.440
calms my jitters is rehearsing,

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:37.120
rehearsing it to death.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:42.550
So even if it's just a
5-minute speech or 15, 20-minute speech,

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:47.770
I rehearse it and refine it to
where I don't need a lot of words.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:54.175
But if I need, if I have the
extra time, I certainly can fill it. But,

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:59.027
yeah, I think rehearsing
it and subtracting from

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:04.359
the things I'm saying and only
providing what's needed is how I feel

00:17:05.859 --> 00:17:07.180
more confident going into it.

00:17:09.829 --> 00:17:12.470
- Absolutely. I always
remember that one. And

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:17.600
I've been using lately what
you said, Ted, to shift your--

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:22.700
is it to shift your
nervousness to excitement?

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:23.200
TED: Yep.

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:25.660
Yeah,

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.160
it's like, one of--

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:30.800
if you think of it as
nervousness that disconnects

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:31.980
you from the audience.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:35.060
But if you think of it
as excitement that's more

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.280
fuel for you to connect.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:41.900
- Yeah. No. I definitely
use that one. Last week,

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:45.920
I was giving a maid of honor
speech, and I was thinking of it,

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:48.920
everything I learned from
Articulation and putting that

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:52.220
into the maid of honor
speech too and trying to

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:55.640
shift the nervousness
into excitement.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:01.345
- Another thing is, I
think it's natural to feel nervous.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.420
I think everybody feels
nervous. So if you don't,

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.390
then that's possibly
a different sign.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:12.640
But the other thing is
that if you have practiced,

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:16.430
then as you're
getting up to do the

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.745
actual performance as it were,

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:23.460
remember back that before
you did all that practice,

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.435
things were a lot worse.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:30.500
So you've come a long way
since that first time you even

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.790
thought of doing
this presentation till now.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.420
So if you've done the practice
and you've got that far,

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.260
you're good to go.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:39.680
- Definitely. Deepti, I
see your hand's raised.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:41.840
- This is

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:46.070
a trick that's helped me
because I read it somewhere

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:50.690
that if you're chewing gum
right before your big presentation,

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.150
it kind of tricks your
brain that because you're chewing

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.395
something, you're having lunch,

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.920
nothing must be wrong, you're
just eating like normal.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.370
And maybe it's placebo
effect, maybe it's real,

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.380
but it has helped
me every time.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:05.360
So I carry a tissue
paper right before--

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:09.320
put it in the pocket real quick
before going on the stage.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:12.680
But that's actually
helped my jitters a lot.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:13.830
And maybe it's just takes

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:18.200
all your nervous energy to
chewing. And your jaw hurts

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.900
later, but it's helped
me a little bit.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:25.190
