00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.470
onboarding. And

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:44.420
I was just curious to
learn from you all,

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:48.050
what are some of
your favorite successful onboarding stories

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:50.150
and what made it so great

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:53.600
because I think there's
probably something that we all

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:54.950
could learn from

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.670
hearing those stories. And Jared,

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.280
I'll kick it off with you
because I see you said

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:02.615
something right away here.

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:04.710
JARED: Can you guys hear me OK?

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:05.640
- Yep, I can hear you.

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:08.900
JARED: Sorry. Yeah. No, I
think for me it's just been

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:12.020
every role I've taken if I've

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:15.800
been thrown in the deep end
having that lifeline of a mentor,

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:19.355
