00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:03.220
- Yeah.

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:07.464
So I think one of
my favorite personal onboarding experiences

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:12.850
my boss handed me the sheet of
paper and he was like, OK, tell

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:15.400
me your preferred style
of being approached.

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.290
Tell me what your
pet peeves are.

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:22.210
Tell me what you would have
wanted to tell your last boss

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:23.230
that ticked you off.

00:23:24.370 --> 00:23:28.360
So having those candid
conversations with people is

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:31.270
really important. And then
when I got to Peloton,

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:34.750
one of the things that
our enterprise data team does is

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:38.770
creates a user manual. So
within somebody's first couple

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:41.650
weeks, they go, OK,
here's what makes me tick.

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:46.180
Here's all these things about me
and how to approach me, what

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.220
motivates me, what
are my afraid of,

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:49.630
what am I really
trying to do here.

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:53.980
And we love it. We still
use that practice today,

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:56.740
and it really helps people
break out of their shell and

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:00.760
make connections when we've got
such a large team that's like

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:02.905
40 plus people. It really

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:06.145
breaks the ice there. So
that's a great practice.

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:08.910
- That's really interesting.

00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:12.710
So it's a template that
you give to everybody or--

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:15.830
- It really shouldn't
be. It's really like we

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:20.120
keep them archived so everybody
can access them on our Google

00:24:20.120 --> 00:24:23.690
Drive. But we want people
to make it their own,

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:25.175
and have fun with it, and

00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:28.760
whatever is going to
help us understand their personality

00:24:28.760 --> 00:24:29.420
and how they work.

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:32.090
- Well. Thank you.

00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:37.586
Mark, I think I saw something
