00:40:10.710 --> 00:40:12.790
But we started small.

00:40:12.790 --> 00:40:15.210
I'd say a couple of things
that we've always tried to emphasize

00:40:15.210 --> 00:40:18.990
is that all levels of skills
and ability are welcome.

00:40:18.990 --> 00:40:21.135
So we've got some folks
who come in and bring

00:40:21.870 --> 00:40:23.535
neural networks and

00:40:24.510 --> 00:40:29.175
self-learning maps and just
really complicated financial topics.

00:40:29.760 --> 00:40:31.680
We've got PhDs
presenting back to us.

00:40:33.270 --> 00:40:36.390
The specifics of which are
probably over a lot of people's

00:40:36.390 --> 00:40:39.000
heads, but everyone finds
it really interesting.

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:42.810
But we also encourage the
person who just learned how to

00:40:42.810 --> 00:40:45.165
do something cool in

00:40:46.380 --> 00:40:48.660
R, in dplyr, in
Python, whatever it is,

00:40:48.660 --> 00:40:49.830
if you've just
learned the basics.

00:40:50.520 --> 00:40:51.750
We had somebody who was--

00:40:51.750 --> 00:40:53.610
I was just posting about
something I was pretty proud of.

00:40:53.610 --> 00:40:56.460
We had a user who figured out
how to connect to our big data

00:40:56.460 --> 00:40:58.950
environment via Python rather
than using the console.

00:40:59.520 --> 00:41:00.510
Those are just small wins.

00:41:00.510 --> 00:41:04.440
So if you can include everyone,
I think is really good chance,

00:41:04.440 --> 00:41:06.570
plus giving everyone a
chance to present too.

00:41:06.570 --> 00:41:09.270
There's so many folks out there
that the way that they really

00:41:09.270 --> 00:41:12.810
learn and really expand is
by pushing themselves to present

00:41:12.810 --> 00:41:15.990
even if it's something
that they just learned themselves

00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:18.570
that might be on the
more basic end. So

00:41:19.470 --> 00:41:20.590
that's really helped.

00:41:20.590 --> 00:41:23.505
And I remember five years
ago when we started this,

00:41:24.510 --> 00:41:27.840
the R and Python community here
was just so fractured and so

00:41:27.840 --> 00:41:28.920
small. And you really had to--

00:41:29.910 --> 00:41:33.060
mainly it was basically Google
and Stack Overflow to figure

00:41:33.060 --> 00:41:35.580
